.TH GETRUSAGE 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
getrusage \- read resource usage
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/resource.h>
.B int getrusage(int who, struct rusage* usage);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads Linux resource usage for RUSAGE_SELF, RUSAGE_CHILDREN, or RUSAGE_THREAD.
The structure uses the Linux x86\-64 ABI.  Crunch uses the POSIX int selector;
GNU libc with GNU extensions declares an enum selector instead.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns zero, or \-1 with errno set.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wait4 (3crunch),
.BR getrusage (2)
